  "text": "A running participant of a debate has no seat where its report is known from nothing the board reads: a macOS `codex exec` (no `/proc`, so no arguments), a `claude -p` run whose output a shell `>` redirect writes to the report (no path in the instruction or the arguments), a relative `-o` (the run's folder is not trusted); the seat comes once the run is over and its record says where the report went."
 },
 "X-MAC-LIVE": {
  "module": "lineage/link",
  "text": "On macOS a running `codex exec` run is not tied to its rollout (`ps` does not say which file it holds open): it is not linked to the thread that started it and is not a page of its own team, so nothing of it is known until the run is over."
 }
},
